  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Don't Laugh, I Love You**: rare: 9 archived performances [9]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2016-02-12.ck930.flac16a** (recommended): source not stated; 33 songs; 146 min; rated 4/5 by 6 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer says the Beyerdynamic mics gave the recording a good sound, as usual for this taper; Reviewer judges this audience recording far better than the church-audio Tascam rig they considered bringing [4][6]\n- **ween2016-02-12.beyer.ck930.flac24**: source not stated; 33 songs; 146 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- This was Ween's first show after a breakup or hiatus of more than four years [1]\n- Confetti guns were aimed straight at the microphones and fired for roughly a minute [1]\n- Confetti guns aimed at the mics went off for about a minute; show followed a 4+ year hiatus [2]\n- The confetti cannon went off just as Deaner started his solo [6]\n- Reviewer says this was Ween's first show in almost five years [6]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2016-02-12.ck930.flac16a**: taped by Mike B; transferred by Mike B; source: Beyerdynamic CK930 > Naiant Tinybox > Sony M10 (@24/48) [1]. Also: This is the 16-bit version for CD burning; a 24-bit version also exists [1]\n- **ween2016-02-12.beyer.ck930.flac24**: taped by Mike B; transferred by Mike B; source: Beyerdynamic CK930 > Naiant Tinybox > Sony M10 (@24/48) [2]. Also: Processed in Wavelab 6.0 with Waves Q10 EQ and L3 maximizer, then tracked, FLAC level 8 encoded and tagged in foobar2000 [2]",
